WEBVTT

00:00:09.503 --> 00:00:10.504
You nailed it, honey.

00:00:10.587 --> 00:00:12.923
Your dad is going to love this!

00:00:13.006 --> 00:00:14.841
Best summer vacation ever!

00:00:14.925 --> 00:00:16.718
Wait till you see the itinerary.

00:00:18.261 --> 00:00:19.638
That's nice.

00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:22.349
Frank, "fire bad." Remember?

00:00:22.432 --> 00:00:25.101
Yeah, right, but maybe you'll find

00:00:25.185 --> 00:00:27.562
your own fireworks on the cruise, huh?

00:00:27.646 --> 00:00:29.648
It's not the Love Boat, Frank.

00:00:29.731 --> 00:00:32.734
I'm just here to have fun
with my family.

00:00:40.742 --> 00:00:41.785
Ahoy there!

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.245
Welcome aboard!

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:53.547
Who is that?

00:00:58.134 --> 00:01:00.220
I am Captain Ericka.

00:01:00.303 --> 00:01:03.181
And, yes, I'm human.
But don't hold that against me.

00:01:03.265 --> 00:01:06.268
I could not be more excited
to have all of you on board

00:01:06.351 --> 00:01:08.937
our first-ever monster cruise!

00:01:18.154 --> 00:01:19.698
Dad? Are you okay?

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.160
No! He's having a heart attack!

00:01:24.244 --> 00:01:25.745
Drac? Not likely.

00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:28.415
Yeah, the only heart attack that can
hurt him is with a wooden stake.

00:01:28.498 --> 00:01:29.541
It must be a stroke!

00:01:29.624 --> 00:01:31.585
Actually, I think it might be her.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.462
Watch where you're pointing, mister,
I'm right here.

00:01:34.629 --> 00:01:36.339
You always stand so close to me.

00:01:36.423 --> 00:01:37.424
It's creepy.

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:41.469
For so long, monsters were hiding,
living in the shadows,

00:01:41.553 --> 00:01:43.013
but not anymore!

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:47.434
You've stood up and waved your hand
or claw or tentacle

00:01:47.517 --> 00:01:52.397
and said, "We're here, we're hairy,
and it is our right to be scary!"

00:01:55.525 --> 00:01:57.861
Now it's time to celebrate!

00:01:58.028 --> 00:02:01.072
You'll enjoy gourmet dining,
thrilling adventures,

00:02:01.156 --> 00:02:02.782
and nonstop entertainment,

00:02:02.866 --> 00:02:05.911
all on the way to our final destination,

00:02:05.994 --> 00:02:09.039
the lost city that isn't lost anymore,

00:02:09.122 --> 00:02:11.541
Atlantis!

00:02:16.129 --> 00:02:17.380
Yeah!

00:02:19.716 --> 00:02:21.176
The fish are acrobats!

00:02:21.259 --> 00:02:22.510
They're fishcrobats!

00:02:26.181 --> 00:02:27.933
Hello. How y'all doing?

00:02:29.643 --> 00:02:30.685
So...

00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:34.230
You must be the one and only Dracula.

00:02:35.982 --> 00:02:39.027
I have waited so long to meet you.

00:02:39.861 --> 00:02:41.613
You really don't age, do you?

00:02:41.696 --> 00:02:43.156
I would kill for your skin.

00:02:46.952 --> 00:02:48.328
You're speaking Transylvanian.

00:02:48.411 --> 00:02:50.205
Always wanted to learn.

00:03:02.092 --> 00:03:03.635
Such a romantic language.

00:03:03.718 --> 00:03:05.679
You know, there's just something
about an accent

00:03:05.762 --> 00:03:08.974
that makes a man sound so intelligent.

00:03:10.725 --> 00:03:12.310
That's Transylvanian right there.

00:03:12.394 --> 00:03:14.437
He's saying it's nice to meet you.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.149
Well, then "alibooboo" to you as well.

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:21.695
Drac! Drac, snap out of it.

00:03:21.778 --> 00:03:23.613
Wait. I've always wanted to do this.

00:03:23.697 --> 00:03:25.699
Wake up! Wake up, Drac!

00:03:25.782 --> 00:03:27.033
Snap out of it!

00:03:27.117 --> 00:03:28.410
Hey, cut it out!

00:03:28.493 --> 00:03:29.786
Hey, buddy, you okay?

00:03:29.869 --> 00:03:32.372
No, not okay.

00:03:32.455 --> 00:03:33.748
Not okay!

00:03:33.915 --> 00:03:35.750
I... I...

00:03:36.084 --> 00:03:37.085
I...

00:03:37.419 --> 00:03:39.129
Zinged.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.617
I went to the moped store,
I said, "Sell it"

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:11.745
Salesman's like,
"What up? What's your budget?"

00:04:11.828 --> 00:04:13.830
And I'm like, "Honestly, I don't know
nothin' about mopeds"

00:04:13.913 --> 00:04:16.124
He said, "I got the one for you,
follow me"

00:04:16.207 --> 00:04:18.209
It's too real

00:04:18.293 --> 00:04:20.587
A chromed-out mirror,
I don't need a windshield

00:04:32.348 --> 00:04:33.516
Check that out!

00:04:40.148 --> 00:04:41.274
Here we go.

00:04:42.525 --> 00:04:43.526
Yummy.

